From 17e3152d911a76e6a9d95ffa41c92a3d21068477 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: subeesh7558 <subeesh.t@focaloid.com>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 18:34:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Backport fix for CVE-2026-6357 to 25.2
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Run pip's self-update check before the command body executes instead
of after. Previously, on commands that install wheels (install, wheel,
download), the post-run version check imported pip's package-finding
machinery — and via lazy imports such as `_manylinux`, those imports
could resolve to modules that the just-installed wheel had placed on
sys.path, giving an attacker code execution via a malicious wheel.

Split self_outdated_check.pip_self_version_check into two halves:

* pip_self_version_check_fetch — does the network/import-heavy work
  to compute the upgrade prompt, called BEFORE the command runs.
* pip_self_version_check_emit — only logs the (already computed)
  prompt, called AFTER the command runs.

Convert Command.handle_pip_version_check / IndexGroupCommand override
to a contextlib.contextmanager-style pip_version_check that performs
the fetch on entry, yields, and emits on exit. InstallCommand also
overrides pip_version_check to skip the self-check entirely when pip
itself is a requirement (the running pip may be replaced before emit).
ListCommand only enters the parent context manager when --outdated or
--uptodate is in play. Update the unit tests accordingly.

Backported from upstream pypa/pip#13923:
  8786d084768e0b42afa093083c8c05ee8e525574  Split the pip self-version
                                            check to get info before run
  378af645dcda1b373c7749d117b69851d506398d  Address review on self-check
                                            split

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
